00:01:17.731 --> 00:01:18.564
30?

00:01:18.564 --> 00:01:19.397
New 25?

00:01:19.397 --> 00:01:20.230
- I don't know.

00:01:20.230 --> 00:01:21.063
I feel like, in this industry-

00:01:21.063 --> 00:01:22.030
- All y'all are laughing,

00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:22.876
like nobody says that.

00:01:22.876 --> 00:01:25.431
(everyone laughing)

00:01:25.431 --> 00:01:26.264
But the thing is-

00:01:26.264 --> 00:01:27.387
- I feel young cause this industry.

00:01:27.387 --> 00:01:28.397
Everybody's always a different age.

00:01:28.397 --> 00:01:29.230
- You're right.

00:01:29.230 --> 00:01:30.063
- Like my whole life,

00:01:30.063 --> 00:01:30.896
even in the industry,

00:01:30.896 --> 00:01:31.729
I've been friends with people

00:01:31.729 --> 00:01:32.839
that are much older than me

00:01:32.839 --> 00:01:33.672
and much younger than me.

00:01:33.672 --> 00:01:35.224
So it's just a weird industry.

00:01:35.224 --> 00:01:36.712
- I will say that fiber

00:01:36.712 --> 00:01:38.093
has become my best friend.

00:01:38.093 --> 00:01:39.508
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:39.508 --> 00:01:40.341
I was like,

00:01:40.341 --> 00:01:42.415
what is this nonsense that I have to do?

00:01:42.415 --> 00:01:44.168
I was like 40 must be like really-

00:01:44.168 --> 00:01:45.953
I had a whole celebration

00:01:45.953 --> 00:01:47.729
when my Squatty Potty came in the mail.

00:01:47.729 --> 00:01:49.612
I was like, "Yes!"

00:01:49.612 --> 00:01:51.695
- I love a Squatty Potty!

00:01:53.237 --> 00:01:55.904
- It's like a revelation, right?

00:01:57.054 --> 00:01:58.429
- My mom is gonna kill me.

00:01:58.429 --> 00:02:00.081
So when my mom as a kid,

00:02:00.081 --> 00:02:00.919
I would walk in, I'd be like,

00:02:00.919 --> 00:02:01.752
"Why are your feet on the-"

00:02:01.752 --> 00:02:03.570
We're short, right?

00:02:03.570 --> 00:02:05.523
We just dangle everywhere.

00:02:05.523 --> 00:02:06.356
We have no legs.

00:02:06.356 --> 00:02:07.522
- Just feet dangling off the toilet?

00:02:07.522 --> 00:02:08.570
- And so she always
had her feet prompt up.

00:02:08.570 --> 00:02:09.403
And then I learned when I was pregnant,

00:02:09.403 --> 00:02:10.236
that they had this thing

00:02:10.236 --> 00:02:11.069
called this Squatty Potty

00:02:11.069 --> 00:02:12.823
and I was like, "Get yourself one!"

00:02:12.823 --> 00:02:14.450
- She's gonna get
everyone Squatty Potties.

00:02:14.450 --> 00:02:16.317
- It's the most amazing invention.

00:02:16.317 --> 00:02:17.283
- It's the best invention ever.

00:02:17.283 --> 00:02:18.299
- It's literally just something you-

00:02:18.299 --> 00:02:20.826
- I find that like getting older,

00:02:20.826 --> 00:02:23.693
like 40, I find joy in random things

00:02:23.693 --> 00:02:25.587
like going to Bed Bath &amp; Beyond

00:02:25.587 --> 00:02:27.456
is a different thing.

00:02:27.456 --> 00:02:28.602
- Organizing.

00:02:28.602 --> 00:02:29.994
- Returns are a different thing.

00:02:29.994 --> 00:02:30.979
(audience laughs)

00:02:30.979 --> 00:02:31.870
You know what I mean?

00:02:31.870 --> 00:02:33.161
I was like, "This is really great."

00:02:33.161 --> 00:02:34.245
- [Kelly] Your knees are different.

00:02:34.245 --> 00:02:36.695
- Our knees are different, Kelly!

00:02:36.695 --> 00:02:37.528
I was like,

00:02:37.528 --> 00:02:39.191
"Oh, I'm not bending over to tie my shoes.

00:02:39.191 --> 00:02:41.368
I'm gonna sit down and
bring my foot to me."

00:02:41.368 --> 00:02:42.487
(Kelly and audience laughs)

00:02:42.487 --> 00:02:44.542
It's just like, I'm not doing that.

00:02:44.542 --> 00:02:45.579
But it's really fun

00:02:45.579 --> 00:02:46.920
because now I feel like

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:48.000
I can just tell everybody,

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:49.430
"Well, I'm your elder."

00:02:49.430 --> 00:02:50.887
- [Kelly] Yeah. Listen to me.

00:02:50.887 --> 00:02:51.874
- People who are like 38,

00:02:51.874 --> 00:02:53.361
I'm like, "I'm your elder."

00:02:53.361 --> 00:02:54.749
So I'm like, "Shut up."

00:02:54.749 --> 00:02:55.643
You know?

00:02:55.643 --> 00:02:57.309
And I need to slow down on that.

00:02:57.309 --> 00:02:58.440
But yeah, it's my birthday.

00:02:58.440 --> 00:02:59.381
I'm excited.

00:02:59.381 --> 00:03:01.046
I usually get a little nervous 'cause-

00:03:01.046 --> 00:03:02.257
I mean, you all know how many days

00:03:02.257 --> 00:03:03.357
in March there are, right?

00:03:03.357 --> 00:03:04.545
How many days?

00:03:04.545 --> 00:03:05.378
- [Kelly] What do you mean?

00:03:05.378 --> 00:03:06.211
- [Brian] 31!

00:03:06.211 --> 00:03:07.044
So, thank you.

00:03:07.044 --> 00:03:07.921
Most of my friends-

00:03:07.921 --> 00:03:09.475
The knuckles, Kelly!

00:03:09.475 --> 00:03:11.356
So most of the people,

00:03:11.356 --> 00:03:12.657
most of my friends never remember

00:03:12.657 --> 00:03:13.954
that there's 31 days in March.

00:03:13.954 --> 00:03:15.193
So I always get my birthday gifts

00:03:15.193 --> 00:03:16.879
a day early or a day late

00:03:16.879 --> 00:03:18.640
and a day late is April Fools.

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:19.571
- Oh.

00:03:19.571 --> 00:03:22.883
- So they always give me
pranks or trash gifts.

00:03:22.883 --> 00:03:23.716
- They're not good friends.

00:03:23.716 --> 00:03:25.141
- I'm not trying to be mean to my friends.

00:03:25.141 --> 00:03:25.974
I'm really not.

00:03:25.974 --> 00:03:28.828
But like, y'all know what y'all do.

00:03:28.828 --> 00:03:29.661
But yeah.

00:03:29.661 --> 00:03:30.725
So I'm always trying to make sure

00:03:30.725 --> 00:03:33.194
people remember there's 31 days in March.

00:03:33.194 --> 00:03:34.188
And no one ever,

00:03:34.188 --> 00:03:35.221
including my family,

00:03:35.221 --> 00:03:36.865
they're calling March 30th

00:03:36.865 --> 00:03:39.357
and I'm like, "That's early."

00:03:39.357 --> 00:03:40.678
Or they'll forget.

00:03:40.678 --> 00:03:41.511
But-

00:03:41.511 --> 00:03:42.344
(audience laughs)

00:03:42.344 --> 00:03:43.533
- And you're like, "Fine."

00:03:43.533 --> 00:03:44.949
- [Brian] Yeah. Fine. Cool.

00:03:44.949 --> 00:03:45.782
- No, the knuckle thing.

00:03:45.782 --> 00:03:46.615
- Yes, the knuckles.

00:03:46.615 --> 00:03:48.804
Do you also know the knuckles for,

00:03:48.804 --> 00:03:49.637
what is it?

00:03:49.637 --> 00:03:52.022
Do you know the nine times tables?

00:03:52.022 --> 00:03:52.904
- Wait, what?

00:03:52.904 --> 00:03:53.737
- Okay.

00:03:53.737 --> 00:03:54.570
So like to give like-

00:03:54.570 --> 00:03:55.403
Yeah, you know, nine times tables.

00:03:55.403 --> 00:03:57.641
So if I wanted to do nine times five,

00:03:57.641 --> 00:03:59.690
you go 1, 2, 3, 4, 5,

00:03:59.690 --> 00:04:00.527
45.

00:04:00.527 --> 00:04:01.360
See 4,

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:02.193
5.

00:04:02.193 --> 00:04:03.153
Nine times seven.

00:04:03.153 --> 00:04:04.736
1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7

00:04:05.809 --> 00:04:06.743
is 63.

00:04:06.743 --> 00:04:07.676
- Why didn't no one tell me this

00:04:07.676 --> 00:04:09.399
when I was a kid?

00:04:09.399 --> 00:04:10.766
See, it's not helping you.

00:04:10.766 --> 00:04:11.767
- Because I'm old!

00:04:11.767 --> 00:04:12.600
I'm 40!

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:14.414
(Kelly and audience laughs)

00:04:14.414 --> 00:04:15.533
- I don't have to do that anymore.

00:04:15.533 --> 00:04:16.366
- You don't have to do that anymore.

00:04:16.366 --> 00:04:17.956
Who uses multiplication?

00:04:17.956 --> 00:04:19.318
- Phone a friend for your homework.

00:04:19.318 --> 00:04:20.491
- That's what's gonna be a problem,

00:04:20.491 --> 00:04:22.255
I'm just gonna start saying things like,

00:04:22.255 --> 00:04:24.796
"Who needs a wallet? I'm 40.

00:04:24.796 --> 00:04:26.434
Who needs ice? I'm 40.

00:04:26.434 --> 00:04:27.293
Me, I need ice.

00:04:27.293 --> 00:04:28.126
'Cause I'm 40."

00:04:28.126 --> 00:04:28.959
But yeah.

00:04:28.959 --> 00:04:29.792
(audience applauds)

00:04:29.792 --> 00:04:31.267
- You're back for season
3 of Atlanta on FX.

00:04:31.267 --> 00:04:33.363
So you took years off between seasons.

00:04:33.363 --> 00:04:34.196
- Yeah. We took a while.

00:04:34.196 --> 00:04:35.029
We took a while.

00:04:35.029 --> 00:04:36.277
- Was it weird to jump
back into character?

00:04:36.277 --> 00:04:38.557
- I was terrified because

00:04:38.557 --> 00:04:40.354
the way we left Alfred in season 2

00:04:40.354 --> 00:04:41.673
was in Robbin season, you know?

00:04:41.673 --> 00:04:43.026
So we had him running through woods,

00:04:43.026 --> 00:04:44.798
being shot at, we had him going

00:04:44.798 --> 00:04:46.892
to all different kind of crazy things.

00:04:46.892 --> 00:04:48.462
And so, I, Brian,

00:04:48.462 --> 00:04:50.110
know that I had changed a lot.

00:04:50.110 --> 00:04:52.104
I had done a lot of growing up,

00:04:52.104 --> 00:04:54.299
I guess you should say.

00:04:54.299 --> 00:04:55.132
And I was like,

00:04:55.132 --> 00:04:56.272
"Well, where's Alfred now?"

00:04:56.272 --> 00:04:57.527
This is literally almost

00:04:57.527 --> 00:04:58.514
four years in the making.

00:04:58.514 --> 00:04:59.475
And I just realized,

00:04:59.475 --> 00:05:00.308
I was like,

00:05:00.308 --> 00:05:01.141
"Well, just lean in.

00:05:01.141 --> 00:05:01.988
Wherever you are that's where Alfred is."

00:05:01.988 --> 00:05:04.827
Except that he's in Europe now.

00:05:04.827 --> 00:05:06.727
I was like, they dropped you in Europe.

00:05:06.727 --> 00:05:08.917
So it was an incredible experience

00:05:08.917 --> 00:05:09.909
because at this time

00:05:09.909 --> 00:05:11.521
we were filming during the lockdown.

00:05:11.521 --> 00:05:13.268
- [Kelly] Yeah, which
is lucky to get to work-

00:05:13.268 --> 00:05:14.101
- It was amazing because

00:05:14.101 --> 00:05:15.939
the last thing they should have done

00:05:15.939 --> 00:05:17.496
is let our black asses
run around in Europe

00:05:17.496 --> 00:05:18.911
(audience laughs)

00:05:18.911 --> 00:05:20.748
because we had the time of our lives.

00:05:20.748 --> 00:05:24.046
Like it really welcoming
and really amazing.

00:05:24.046 --> 00:05:25.992
Like it was just so calm and serene

00:05:25.992 --> 00:05:26.834
and then the four of us

00:05:26.834 --> 00:05:28.871
were more together this season.

00:05:28.871 --> 00:05:30.944
Because we were the only people there

00:05:30.944 --> 00:05:32.034
that we could depend on in that way-

00:05:32.034 --> 00:05:32.867
- In your bubble.

00:05:32.867 --> 00:05:33.700
- In our bubble.

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:34.948
So we were together a lot.

00:05:34.948 --> 00:05:36.950
We celebrated my birthday there.

00:05:36.950 --> 00:05:38.907
Donald threw me a tattoo party,

00:05:38.907 --> 00:05:40.434
which was really nice.

00:05:40.434 --> 00:05:41.267
- Oh wait, was that a good decision

00:05:41.267 --> 00:05:42.100
or a bad decision?

00:05:42.100 --> 00:05:42.933
- It was my decision!

00:05:42.933 --> 00:05:43.766
That's all that matters.

00:05:43.766 --> 00:05:45.559
Like we're all getting tattoos so-

00:05:45.559 --> 00:05:46.520
- You're gonna love it!

00:05:46.520 --> 00:05:48.546
- And we all got matching
Atlanta A tattoos.

00:05:48.546 --> 00:05:50.419
- Oh, I like it!

00:05:50.419 --> 00:05:51.252
- Not Zazie, though.

00:05:51.252 --> 00:05:53.676
She was like, "I'm not playing that game."

00:05:53.676 --> 00:05:56.226
But we all got matching tattoos.

00:05:56.226 --> 00:05:57.111
It was really great.

00:05:57.111 --> 00:05:58.994
This season's unlike anything

00:05:58.994 --> 00:06:00.207
we've ever done before.

00:06:00.207 --> 00:06:01.040
- Where were you in Europe?

00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:02.798
- We were in London, for the most part.

00:06:02.798 --> 00:06:04.071
And then we were in Amsterdam

00:06:04.071 --> 00:06:05.783
and then we did a little
bit of time in Paris.

00:06:05.783 --> 00:06:07.390
So there were certain buildings

00:06:07.390 --> 00:06:08.523
and museums and stuff

00:06:08.523 --> 00:06:09.889
that we could just run rampant in

00:06:09.889 --> 00:06:10.761
because nobody was there

00:06:10.761 --> 00:06:12.056
and they were like, "Yeah, sure. Go."

00:06:12.056 --> 00:06:12.889
And I was like,

00:06:12.889 --> 00:06:14.054
"Oh, this is really, really great."

00:06:14.054 --> 00:06:15.156
- Kind of cool 'cause-

00:06:15.156 --> 00:06:16.070
- It was unbelievable.

00:06:16.070 --> 00:06:17.146
It was unbelievable.

00:06:17.146 --> 00:06:18.413
Yeah. It wouldn't have been the case.

00:06:18.413 --> 00:06:19.246
It was great.

00:06:19.246 --> 00:06:20.576
- So you went to school in Atlanta, right?

00:06:20.576 --> 00:06:21.899
- I did go to school in Atlanta.

00:06:21.899 --> 00:06:23.565
I went to Morehouse College.

00:06:23.565 --> 00:06:24.398
- Morehouse College. All right.

00:06:24.398 --> 00:06:25.856
You like going there?

00:06:25.856 --> 00:06:27.084
You like living there?

00:06:27.084 --> 00:06:27.917
- I like going there

00:06:27.917 --> 00:06:30.125
but let me tell you something.

00:06:30.125 --> 00:06:30.958
I hate it.

00:06:30.958 --> 00:06:32.527
I was a (beep) in college.

00:06:32.527 --> 00:06:33.360
I have to say it.

00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:34.193
That's what I was.

00:06:34.193 --> 00:06:35.026
I really was.

00:06:35.026 --> 00:06:36.062
That's the only way I could put it.

00:06:36.062 --> 00:06:38.751
I was very much an activist.

00:06:38.751 --> 00:06:40.607
I feel like I was in one
of those 1980s movies

00:06:40.607 --> 00:06:42.092
where the Dean calls you in and is like,

00:06:42.092 --> 00:06:43.993
"What are you rebel against today, Henry?"

00:06:43.993 --> 00:06:46.287
And I'm like, "What do you got?"

00:06:46.287 --> 00:06:47.191
- Just say something.

00:06:47.191 --> 00:06:49.221
- Just tell me what it is!

00:06:49.221 --> 00:06:50.386
and that's who I was.

00:06:50.386 --> 00:06:51.268
- You were on a mission.

00:06:51.268 --> 00:06:52.101
- I was on a mission.

00:06:52.101 --> 00:06:52.934
I was like,

00:06:52.934 --> 00:06:55.360
this is the only all black male college

00:06:55.360 --> 00:06:56.452
in the country.

00:06:56.452 --> 00:06:57.285
You know?

00:06:57.285 --> 00:06:58.389
Like you've got all these young black men

00:06:58.389 --> 00:07:00.232
coming from all different
parts of the country.

00:07:00.232 --> 00:07:01.381
From the world, really.

00:07:01.381 --> 00:07:02.900
And we're in higher education.

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:03.924
in Atlanta, Georgia.

00:07:03.924 --> 00:07:05.813
And I was like, "I wanna rebel."

00:07:05.813 --> 00:07:08.101
So I grew my hair out.

00:07:08.101 --> 00:07:08.934
You know what I mean?

00:07:08.934 --> 00:07:10.253
I got my ears pierced.

00:07:10.253 --> 00:07:11.086
I had tattoos.

00:07:11.086 --> 00:07:11.919
I would wear-

00:07:11.919 --> 00:07:13.225
I was insane.

00:07:13.225 --> 00:07:15.106
- I feel like this is
what people do in college?

00:07:15.106 --> 00:07:16.092
- You would think so

00:07:16.092 --> 00:07:17.749
but Morehouse is very much,

00:07:17.749 --> 00:07:18.582
it's prestigious.

00:07:18.582 --> 00:07:19.780
It's like, you wear suits

00:07:19.780 --> 00:07:21.818
and you're supposed to be

00:07:21.818 --> 00:07:24.447
an upstanding young
black man in the country.

00:07:24.447 --> 00:07:28.664
And my ass was just
running around this campus

00:07:28.664 --> 00:07:31.016
just doing stupid stuff!

00:07:31.016 --> 00:07:32.946
Like I was doing stupid stuff!

00:07:32.946 --> 00:07:33.779
I'm really grateful

00:07:33.779 --> 00:07:35.276
that I'm a notable alumni now

00:07:35.276 --> 00:07:37.449
and I hope it stays that way

00:07:37.449 --> 00:07:38.776
but I was trash.

00:07:38.776 --> 00:07:40.676
(everyone laughs)

00:07:40.676 --> 00:07:41.759
- I love you so much.

00:07:41.759 --> 00:07:42.592
- But I had a great time.

00:07:42.592 --> 00:07:45.208
I still have the same
friends from college.

00:07:45.208 --> 00:07:47.338
I ran the streets of Atlanta back then.

00:07:47.338 --> 00:07:48.171
So it's like-

00:07:48.171 --> 00:07:49.004
- You're very self aware,

00:07:49.004 --> 00:07:49.837
that amazing.

00:07:49.837 --> 00:07:50.670
- [Brian] I had to be!

00:07:50.670 --> 00:07:51.603
'Cause I was a mess!

00:07:51.603 --> 00:07:52.625
I was a mess.

00:07:52.625 --> 00:07:53.458
I was a mess at college.

00:07:53.458 --> 00:07:54.611
- I think we all were messes.

00:07:54.611 --> 00:07:55.857
Especially was in our early 20s.

00:07:55.857 --> 00:07:56.690
- [Brian] This was
different though, Kelly.

00:07:56.690 --> 00:07:57.523
This was-

00:07:57.523 --> 00:07:58.466
This guy was-

00:07:58.466 --> 00:07:59.446
This was different.

00:07:59.446 --> 00:08:00.279
- [Kelly] Oh man.

00:08:00.279 --> 00:08:01.328
I kind of wish I could have met him.

00:08:01.328 --> 00:08:02.911
- Oh, man.

00:08:02.911 --> 00:08:03.744
He's 40 now.

00:08:03.744 --> 00:08:04.952
(audience laughs)

00:08:04.952 --> 00:08:05.785
He's 40 now.

00:08:05.785 --> 00:08:06.618
I can't.

00:08:06.618 --> 00:08:07.451
- Okay. Wait.

00:08:07.451 --> 00:08:08.284
I don't wanna not talk about this

00:08:08.284 --> 00:08:09.117
'cause you've also got a crime movie

00:08:09.117 --> 00:08:10.045
with Brad Pitt.

00:08:10.045 --> 00:08:11.063
- Yeah.

00:08:11.063 --> 00:08:12.344
- So it's out this summer?

00:08:12.344 --> 00:08:13.177
- Yeah.

00:08:13.177 --> 00:08:14.010
- So what's that about?

00:08:14.010 --> 00:08:14.843
- You know,

00:08:14.843 --> 00:08:16.274
I've always had a dream

00:08:16.274 --> 00:08:18.704
of being in an action movie

00:08:18.704 --> 00:08:21.220
where you get all the explosions

00:08:21.220 --> 00:08:22.691
and the slow motion walk,

00:08:22.691 --> 00:08:23.524
you know what I mean?

00:08:23.524 --> 00:08:24.357
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:08:24.357 --> 00:08:25.190
- And I gotta do it

00:08:25.190 --> 00:08:26.023
and I gotta do it with Brad Pitt.

00:08:26.023 --> 00:08:29.108
And I was like, "I know you lying."

00:08:29.108 --> 00:08:29.941
Yeah.

00:08:29.941 --> 00:08:30.905
And I got to be blonde.

00:08:30.905 --> 00:08:31.738
I was like,

00:08:31.738 --> 00:08:34.491
"Yes! I get to be blonde-"

00:08:34.491 --> 00:08:35.324
- So you're still rebelling.

00:08:35.324 --> 00:08:36.304
- I'm still rebelling!

00:08:36.304 --> 00:08:37.263
(everyone laughs)

00:08:37.263 --> 00:08:38.211
That is literally kind what

00:08:38.211 --> 00:08:39.272
my hair look like in college.

00:08:39.272 --> 00:08:40.105
And I was like,

00:08:40.105 --> 00:08:42.177
"Oh, that's a little too close to home."

00:08:42.177 --> 00:08:43.010
But yeah,

00:08:43.010 --> 00:08:44.586
it's a great, great
film called Bullet Train

00:08:44.586 --> 00:08:46.154
directed by David Leitch who did like,

00:08:46.154 --> 00:08:47.081
you know,

00:08:47.081 --> 00:08:49.030
Atomic Blonde and Deadpool.

00:08:49.030 --> 00:08:51.331
And we did this in the
middle of the quarantine.

00:08:51.331 --> 00:08:53.164
So like in October-

00:08:53.164 --> 00:08:54.653
- But you worked all in quarantine?

00:08:54.653 --> 00:08:55.577
That's cool.

00:08:55.577 --> 00:08:56.511
- I'm insane.

00:08:56.511 --> 00:08:57.865
I told you I was a rebel.

00:08:57.865 --> 00:08:58.934
- I work too.

00:08:58.934 --> 00:08:59.786
I never stopped either.

00:08:59.786 --> 00:09:01.369
- I know!

00:09:01.369 --> 00:09:02.514
- It was a nice distraction.

00:09:02.514 --> 00:09:03.372
- I feel like I need
to be interviewing you

00:09:03.372 --> 00:09:05.242
so you can have a break.

00:09:05.242 --> 00:09:06.075
- Trust me. I'm tired.

00:09:06.075 --> 00:09:07.605
I'm gonna have a weekend.

00:09:07.605 --> 00:09:09.063
- Don't switch.

00:09:09.063 --> 00:09:09.896
- It's kind of nice though,

00:09:09.896 --> 00:09:10.729
because I don't feel

00:09:10.729 --> 00:09:11.675
like I was affected during quarantine

00:09:11.675 --> 00:09:13.806
like everybody else was, in that sense.

00:09:13.806 --> 00:09:15.725
Because I had to still keep going

00:09:15.725 --> 00:09:16.776
so there was no time to process.

00:09:16.776 --> 00:09:17.948
- It was the same with Bullet Train.

00:09:17.948 --> 00:09:19.255
We filmed on Sony.

00:09:19.255 --> 00:09:20.246
They built a train.

00:09:20.246 --> 00:09:22.510
Like they built cars of the train.

00:09:22.510 --> 00:09:23.349
There was a huge screen

00:09:23.349 --> 00:09:25.432
with moving pictures going.

00:09:25.432 --> 00:09:27.102
I felt like it was very classic Hollywood

00:09:27.102 --> 00:09:28.000
like back in the 20s

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:29.883
when there was like 30 people moving a set

00:09:29.883 --> 00:09:31.144
and turning this.

00:09:31.144 --> 00:09:32.343
You had to get back to the bare minimum.

00:09:32.343 --> 00:09:34.539
But yeah, it's a huge action movie.

00:09:34.539 --> 00:09:35.927
The cast is insane.

00:09:35.927 --> 00:09:37.642
And I got to fight Brad Pitt.

00:09:37.642 --> 00:09:39.921
Like I get to kick Brad Pitt's ass.

00:09:39.921 --> 00:09:41.045
(everyone laughs)

00:09:41.045 --> 00:09:42.421
And it was kind of great because,

00:09:42.421 --> 00:09:43.254
I mean,

00:09:43.254 --> 00:09:44.900
this man was the happiest he had ever been

00:09:44.900 --> 00:09:46.076
and also,

00:09:46.076 --> 00:09:48.005
we have a lot of fights together

00:09:48.005 --> 00:09:49.347
and there's one particular time

00:09:49.347 --> 00:09:50.180
that we're fighting

00:09:50.180 --> 00:09:51.332
and I got him in a chokehold

00:09:51.332 --> 00:09:52.323
and like they would yell, "Cut"

00:09:52.323 --> 00:09:53.583
and he would just laying my arms.

00:09:53.583 --> 00:09:55.791
And I was like, "Oh."

00:09:55.791 --> 00:09:56.624
I was like,

00:09:56.624 --> 00:09:59.130
"How is it possible that
I feel safer with you

00:09:59.130 --> 00:09:59.979
lying in my arms?"

00:09:59.979 --> 00:10:01.805
And it's like, 'cause it's Brad Pitt.

00:10:01.805 --> 00:10:02.735
- [Kelly] I love you right now.

00:10:02.735 --> 00:10:03.755
- Yeah, it was great.

00:10:03.755 --> 00:10:04.608
Like all of us,

00:10:04.608 --> 00:10:06.000
Aaron Taylor-Johnson, Joey king,

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:08.246
we all just signed up to have a great time

00:10:08.246 --> 00:10:10.333
and just be bloody and
kick each other's butts-

00:10:10.333 --> 00:10:11.202
- What a fun job.

00:10:11.202 --> 00:10:12.092
- It was the best.

00:10:12.092 --> 00:10:13.793
It didn't feel real.

00:10:13.793 --> 00:10:14.906
It really didn't feel real,

00:10:14.906 --> 00:10:15.790
but it was really great.

00:10:15.790 --> 00:10:17.418
And it's gonna be an amazing movie.

00:10:17.418 --> 00:10:18.453
- I'm excited.

00:10:18.453 --> 00:10:19.375
I love action films.

00:10:19.375 --> 00:10:20.208
- Yeah, me too.

00:10:20.208 --> 00:10:21.252
- [Kelly] I love them.

